<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hyderabad State Congress</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1938">1938</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hyderabad State Congress was a political party founded in 1938 to campaign for responsible government in Hyderabad State. Banned by the Nizam's government, it led satyagraha campaigns, and under Swami Ramananda Tirtha it pressed in 1947–1948 for accession to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. It merged into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-national-congress">Indian National Congress</a> after the state's integration.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Majlis-e-Ittehadul Muslimeen under Qasim Razvi organised the Razakars, a paramilitary force that attacked opponents of the regime and Hindu villages, while the <b>State Congress</b> campaigned for accession and the Communist Party led a peasant insurrection in Telangana against the landlords and the state.</blockquote><a href="/empire/hyderabad-state">Hyderabad State · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
